        <h3 style="font-size: 24pt;">Chemistry department acquires spectrophotometer</h3>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 20px;">The Chemistry Department's most recent equipment acquisition is a new Shimadzu UV-2600 ultraviolet and visible scanning spectrophotometer, replacing our oldest Shimadzu UV-2101 PC UV-vis spectrophotometer. We still maintain two Shimadzu UV-vis scanning spectrophotometers — a UV-2450 along with the UV-2600 — that see regular activity in Physical Chemistry lab, Biochemistry lab, and Instrumental Analysis. In addition, the equipment serves as a key piece of instrumentation for students taking Introduction to Research.</p>
